## Primary Pest Species & Environmental Factors
1. Western Drywood Termites (Incisitermes minor): Coastal winds blow swarmers into roof eaves and rafter tails during late summer and autumn. Diagnosed by hexagonal fecal pellets (frass).
2. Western Subterranean Termites (Reticulitermes hesperus): Moisture-dependent colonies in sandy coastal soil constructing mud shelter tubes over concrete stem walls.
3. Roof Rats (Rattus rattus): Agile climbing rodents utilizing mature palm trees and utility drops to enter attics and wall voids.
4. Argentine Ants (Linepithema humile): Massive multi-queen subterranean supercolonies driven indoors by winter saturation and summer heat.
5. Cockroaches: German cockroaches infesting indoor kitchens; Oriental cockroaches (waterbugs) flourishing in damp coastal vaults and seawalls.
6. Spiders: Western black widows and brown widows nesting under patio furniture, stucco weep screeds, and garage perimeters.

